      "problem": "Given a rectangular solid, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the surface area $S$ of the rectangular solid if the base is a square with the side of $a=3$ and the height is $h=7.$",
      "worked_solution": "The surface area of the given rectangular solid is $S=2{a}^{2}+4ah.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(a,h) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂a})\\,\\text{d}a+(\\frac{∂S}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =(4a+4h)\\,\\text{d}a+4a\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $a=3$ and $h=7,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(3,7) & =(4\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 7)\\,\\text{d}a+4\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =40\\,\\text{d}a+12\\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
